player: publish the video track playback will select as pending-vid

Inside the on_preloaded hook the track list is complete but nothing is
selected yet: select_default_track runs right after the hook, and until
playback is initialized the vid property answers with the option value,
which is "auto" for every ordinary session. A client that must decide
per-file decode routing inside the hook, before the decoder exists (High
10 to software decode on hardware without that profile, Dolby Vision P5
reshaping), cannot tell which of several video tracks it is deciding for
and falls back to the first demuxed one -- wrong for attached pictures,
dual-angle files, a default-flagged second track, --vlang, or an explicit
vid=N.

Add a read-only pending-vid property: before playback initializes it runs
the same selection the player is about to run (honouring --no-stream-auto-sel
and vid=no, with no side effects on the tracks), and afterwards it reports
the selected track like vid. "no" when none will be selected, unavailable
without a file.

diff --git a/DOCS/man/input.rst b/DOCS/man/input.rst
index 24f9d7a..25b42c1 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/input.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/input.rst
@@ -3551,6 +3551,16 @@ Property list
     If tracks of the requested type are selected via ``--lavfi-complex``, the
     first one is returned.
 
+``pending-vid``
+    The ID of the video track playback will select, or ``no``. Unlike ``vid``,
+    which returns the option value (``auto`` as often as not) until playback
+    is initialized, this is answered before the track is selected: inside the
+    ``on_preloaded`` hook it runs the same default selection the player runs
+    right after the hook, so a hook that decides per-file decode routing
+    before the decoder exists knows which track it is deciding for. Once
+    playback is initialized it returns the selected track, like ``vid``.
+    Unavailable when no file is loaded.
+
 ``chapter-list`` (RW)
     List of chapters, current entry marked.
 
